  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 107 PM CST Sun Nov 22 2026\n\nA COLD FRONT, CURRENTLY POSITIONED ALONG A LINE EXTENDING FROM WEST- \nCENTRAL IL TO SOUTH-WESTERN MO, IS PROGRESSING SLOWLY BUT SURELY \nTHROUGH THE AREA. RAIN CONTINUES AHEAD OF IT AS OF 1815Z, \nOVERACHIEVING IN PORTIONS OF MO ALREADY--PRESUMABLY DUE TO SLIGHTLY \nHIGHER THAN EXPECTED PWAT VALUES AND MODEST 500HPA CVA. \nACCUMULATIONS IN SOME OF OUR WESTERN COUNTIES HAVE ALREADY SURPASSED \n0.25\", WITH HIGHEST QPE VALUES NEARING 0.5\" IN BOLLINGER CO. MO. \nWHILE NOT OF ANY CONCERN, THERE ARE A FEW HUNDRED J/KG OF MUCAPE \nAHEAD OF THE LINE INTO WESTERN KY WHICH MAY LEAD TO SOME CONVECTIVE \nGUSTS AND A CLAP OF THUNDER OR TWO. BEHIND THE FRONT THIS EVENING, \n25 KT WIND GUSTS WILL BECOME WIDESPREAD, WITH A FEW EMBEDDED 30 KT \nGUSTS NOT OUT OF THE QUESTION. TEMPERATURES WILL FALL TONIGHT TO \nNEAR-BUT-LIKELY-ABOVE FREEZING IN OUR SOUTHEASTERN COUNTIES INTO \nSOUTHERN IN, AND BELOW FREEZING IN MOST PORTIONS OF SOUTHERN IL AND \nINTO MO. \n\nMONDAY WILL RESTART THE BONA FIDE AUTUMN REGIME, WITH HIGH \nTEMPERATURES HANGING AROUND 50. THE POST-FRONTAL GUSTS WILL CONTINUE \nTOMORROW AS WELL--COMFORTABLY BETWEEN 10 AND 15 KNOTS--FOR THE \nENTIRE AREA. THIS GENERAL PATTERN WILL EXIST THROUGH DAYLIGHT \nTUESDAY.\n\nA SECOND STORM SYSTEM ARRIVES LATE TUESDAY-EARLY WEDNESDAY, WITH \nGOOD AGREEMENT IN MODELS REGARDING THE PLACEMENT OF A DIGGING 250 \nHPA TROUGH. A SURFACE LOW IS LIKELY TO FORM OFF OF THE GULF COAST AT \nTHAT TIME, IN WHICH CASE A NOR'EASTER IS LIKELY TO FORM. WHILE THAT \nWILL NOT IMPACT OUR REGION IMMEDIATELY, ISENTROPIC AND \nQUASIGEOSTROPHIC LIFT ASSOCIATED WITH A CURRENTLY PROGGED CUTOFF UL \nLOW (GFS/ECMWF) WILL STILL BRING WIDESPREAD PRECIPITATION TO THE \nAREA. A FEW MEMBERS OF ENSEMBLE MODELS HAD SOME FLURRIES FALLING ON \nTHE NORTH SIDE OF THE FORECAST AREA, THOUGH THE CHANCES OF THIS ARE \nPROBABILISTICALLY LOW. AT THIS TIME, SOME RAIN IS EXPECTED TO FALL \nTHROUGH THANKSGIVING, BUT NO MAJOR TRAVEL IMPACTS ARE EXPECTED. IF \nRAIN WERE TO FALL WHEN AMBIENT TEMPERATURES ARE BELOW FREEZING, USE \nCAUTION ON OVERPASSES AND BRIDGES. FOR MOST ROADS, GROUND \nTEMPERATURES WILL BE TOO WARM FOR ANY WATER TO STAGNATE AND FREEZE.",
